  "definition": "Change detection uses observations from two or more times to locate differences in a surface state or in its spectral behaviour. The immediate result is an observed difference or a statistical break. Explaining it as construction, fire, flood, vegetation stress or a lasting land-cover conversion is a further inference that usually needs classification and contextual evidence.",
